{
  "id": "FEAT-04-source-tax-liability",
  "order": 4,
  "title": "Decide whether the employee is subject to source tax",
  "goal": "Lonio asks only the questions needed to decide whether an employee is subject to source tax, so that only those employees get the source tax questions and nobody gives nationality, permit or spouse data that is not needed.",
  "context": "HR decides by hand whether an employee is subject to source tax. Employees living abroad always are. Swiss nationals and C permit holders living in Switzerland are not. Other foreigners living in Switzerland are not subject if they are married to a spouse who is Swiss or holds a C permit and lives in Switzerland (F-TR-005, F-TR-006, F-TR-025, F-TR-030, F-TR-034, F-TR-037). Because of data minimisation, each of these questions is asked only when its answer can change the outcome (G-01). The rule uses address_country (FEAT-02) and civil_status (FEAT-03). Nobody has analysed the tariff questions of the Zurich calculator yet (OQ-01, blocking). Until then, this feature only decides whether the employee is subject or not, and that decision controls whether the tariff questions are asked. HR is not sure the rule is complete (OQ-05). The list of permit types is not defined (OQ-06). HR wished for a reminder to bring the permit because half of new employees forget it (F-TR-028, OQ-07). Using the Zurich calculator for every employee is an agreed simplification (F-TR-008, G-05, OQ-08).",
  "stakeholders": [
    "employee",
    "hr",
    "source_tax"
  ],
  "items": [
